# CODEOWNERS — Project Pinnacle VMS
#
# US-01.1.1 · T-01.1.1.2
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENT STATE — single-owner repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is owned by a personal GitHub account, which cannot have
# teams. Every path therefore maps to @mamunulhasan.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: GitHub never requests review from the author of
# a pull request. With one owner, a CODEOWNERS rule can never be satisfied on
# a PR that owner raised. Enabling "require review from Code Owners" on branch
# protection today would block every merge permanently.
#
# So that setting is DEFERRED, not enabled — recorded as a documented
# deviation against US-01.1.1 AC-2 and AC-3. See:
#   docs/project/02-traceability-matrix.md  (delivery log)
#   docs/project/13-branch-protection.md    (deviation register)
#
# This file is still worth having now: it declares ownership intent, and the
# moment a second collaborator or an organisation exists it becomes
# enforceable by flipping one protection setting.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHEN THE TEAM EXISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Move the repository to a `pantropi` organisation, create these teams, then
# replace @mamunulhasan below:
#
#   @pantropi/vms-maintainers  — default owners
#   @pantropi/vms-architects   — architecture, ACS boundary, schema, ADRs
#   @pantropi/vms-security     — auth, RBAC, secrets, audit
#   @pantropi/vms-product      — requirements, traceability, open questions
#
# Then enable "Require review from Code Owners" on `main` and `develop`, and
# raise the ACS/security paths to two required approvals (AC-3).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

